# Miso Honey Broiled Chicken and Asparagus

Sweet, savory, and spicy broiled chicken thighs with asparagus, finished with reserved miso marinade and scallions.

## info

* About 45 minutes
* 4 servings

## ingredients

### Marinade

* 3 tablespoons white miso
* 3 tablespoons mild honey
* 3 tablespoons soy sauce or tamari
* 1 tablespoon rice vinegar
* 2 teaspoons finely grated fresh ginger
* 2 teaspoons finely grated garlic
* 2 teaspoons chile-garlic sauce or other hot sauce
* 1 tablespoon neutral oil
* 1 tablespoon water

### Chicken and Vegetables

* 1½ to 2 pounds boneless, skinless chicken thighs
* 1 large bunch asparagus (about 1 pound), trimmed
* 2 teaspoons neutral oil
* Salt, to taste
* Black pepper, to taste
* 2 scallions, thinly sliced
* Cooked rice, optional, for serving

## steps

1. Make the marinade by whisking together the miso, honey, soy sauce, rice vinegar, ginger, garlic, chile-garlic sauce, 1 tablespoon oil, and 1 tablespoon water. Reserve and refrigerate half of the marinade for serving.

2. Place the chicken in a shallow dish or zip-top bag and pour the remaining marinade over it. Toss to coat evenly. Marinate in the refrigerator for up to 30 minutes.

3. Heat the broiler with a rack positioned about 6 inches below the heat source. Line a large baking sheet with aluminum foil.

4. Remove the chicken from the marinade, scraping off excess marinade. Arrange the chicken in a single layer on one side of the baking sheet with the flatter side facing up.

5. Place the asparagus on the other side of the baking sheet. Drizzle with the remaining 2 teaspoons oil, season with salt and pepper, and toss to coat.

6. Broil for about 10 minutes, until the chicken is cooked through with some charred spots and the asparagus is browned.

7. Transfer to serving plates. Drizzle the reserved marinade over the chicken and garnish with sliced scallions.

8. Serve with cooked rice, if desired.

## notes

* Do not marinate the chicken for much longer than 30 minutes, as the marinade may begin to affect the texture of the meat.
* Reserving half of the marinade before adding the chicken ensures a clean sauce for serving.
* Chicken thighs are more forgiving under the broiler and develop excellent caramelization from the honey and miso.
* For extra char, move the baking sheet closer to the broiler during the last minute of cooking.

